FFT3DFilter R2 (myrsloik/VapourSynth-FFT3DFilter, tag R2 = 50194b4): two
faults that make its output differ from run to run, so a preview never
matches the encode (VapourBox task #62,
docs/reports/task-62-fft3dfilter-determinism).

1. FFT3DFilterTransform.cpp, FramePlaneToCoverbuf: each line of the padded
   cover buffer mirrored its left border BEFORE copying the source line into
   it, so the border was mirrored from the previous frame's pixels (or
   uninitialised heap memory on the first frame). The left 10 luma / 6 chroma
   columns depended on request order. Introduced upstream in da50417
   (2018-01-11, "Turn several functions into templates"); the 2015 original
   copied the line first. Fixed in all three loops (progressive, both fields).

2. FFT3DFilter.cpp, ApplyFilter / Wiener3D: the per-frame Wiener sigma was
   written to the shared member sigmaSquaredNoiseNormed, but the filter is
   fmParallel and the edge frames (btcur 1) write the 2D value while middle
   frames write and read the 3D one (x bt). Two threads interleaving filtered
   a middle frame at 1/bt of its sigma. Now a local in both functions.

Applied by download-deps-{macos,linux}.sh and download-deps-windows.ps1 right
after the clone; each build fails if it stops applying.

diff --git a/FFT3DFilter.cpp b/FFT3DFilter.cpp
index 7686e6a..e5dfdab 100644
--- a/FFT3DFilter.cpp
+++ b/FFT3DFilter.cpp
@@ -303,6 +303,7 @@ void FFT3DFilter::Wiener3D
     VSFrameContext *frame_ctx,
     const VSAPI *vsapi
 ) {
+    const float sigmaSquaredNoiseNormed = btcur * sigma * sigma / norm; /* local: see ApplyFilter */
     int fromframe = n - btcur / 2;
     int outcenter = btcur / 2;
     const fftwf_complex *frames[btcur] = {};
@@ -357,7 +358,7 @@ const VSFrame *FFT3DFilter::ApplyFilter
 
     if (btcur > 0) /* Wiener */
     {
-        sigmaSquaredNoiseNormed = btcur * sigma * sigma / norm; /* normalized variation=sigma^2 */
+        const float sigmaSquaredNoiseNormed = btcur * sigma * sigma / norm; /* normalized variation=sigma^2; a local, not the shared member: frames run in parallel and edge frames use btcur 1 */
 
         /* get power spectral density (abs quadrat) for every block and apply filter */
 
